{
  "id": "m7l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Herencia y __str__",
    "en": "Inheritance and __str__"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Reutilizar con herencia"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Una clase puede **heredar** de otra: recibe sus atributos y métodos, y puede **redefinirlos**. `class Gato(Animal)` hereda de `Animal`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "class Animal:",
          "    def hablar(self):",
          "        return '...'",
          "",
          "class Gato(Animal):",
          "    def hablar(self):",
          "        return 'Miau'",
          "",
          "print(Gato().hablar())"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Miau"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Representación legible: __str__"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "El método especial `__str__` define cómo se ve el objeto al imprimirlo o al convertirlo a texto con `str()`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "class Punto:",
          "    def __init__(self, x, y):",
          "        self.x = x",
          "        self.y = y",
          "    def __str__(self):",
          "        return f'({self.x}, {self.y})'",
          "",
          "print(Punto(3, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "(3, 4)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Existen más métodos especiales (`__eq__`, `__len__`…) que permiten que tus objetos se integren con el lenguaje."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Reuse with inheritance"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A class can **inherit** from another: it gets its attributes and methods, and can **override** them. `class Gato(Animal)` inherits from `Animal`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "class Animal:",
          "    def hablar(self):",
          "        return '...'",
          "",
          "class Gato(Animal):",
          "    def hablar(self):",
          "        return 'Miau'",
          "",
          "print(Gato().hablar())"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Miau"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Readable representation: __str__"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "The special method `__str__` defines how the object looks when printed or converted to text with `str()`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "class Punto:",
          "    def __init__(self, x, y):",
          "        self.x = x",
          "        self.y = y",
          "    def __str__(self):",
          "        return f'({self.x}, {self.y})'",
          "",
          "print(Punto(3, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "(3, 4)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "There are more special methods (`__eq__`, `__len__`…) that let your objects integrate with the language."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m7l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Crea una clase `Animal` con un método `hablar()` que devuelva `'...'`, y una clase `Perro` que herede de `Animal` y redefina `hablar()` para devolver `'Guau'`.",
        "en": "Create a class `Animal` with a method `hablar()` returning `'...'`, and a class `Perro` inheriting from `Animal` that overrides `hablar()` to return `'Guau'`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "class Animal:",
        "    def hablar(self):",
        "        return '...'",
        "",
        "class Perro(Animal):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "class Animal:",
        "    def hablar(self):",
        "        return '...'",
        "",
        "class Perro(Animal):",
        "    def hablar(self):",
        "        return 'Guau'"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Perro(Animal) hereda de Animal.",
          "Redefine hablar() dentro de Perro."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Perro(Animal) inherits from Animal.",
          "Override hablar() inside Perro."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "herencia",
          "harness": "assert Animal().hablar() == '...'\nassert Perro().hablar() == 'Guau'\nassert isinstance(Perro(), Animal)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m7l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Crea una clase `Punto(x, y)` cuyo `str()` devuelva `'(x, y)'`. Ej: `str(Punto(3, 4))` → `'(3, 4)'`.",
        "en": "Create a class `Punto(x, y)` whose `str()` returns `'(x, y)'`. E.g. `str(Punto(3, 4))` → `'(3, 4)'`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "class Punto:",
        "    def __init__(self, x, y):",
        "        pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "class Punto:",
        "    def __init__(self, x, y):",
        "        self.x = x",
        "        self.y = y",
        "    def __str__(self):",
        "        return f'({self.x}, {self.y})'"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Guarda x e y en __init__.",
          "Define __str__ devolviendo una f-string '(x, y)'."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Store x and y in __init__.",
          "Define __str__ returning an f-string '(x, y)'."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "name": "str",
          "harness": "assert str(Punto(3, 4)) == '(3, 4)'\nassert str(Punto(0, -2)) == '(0, -2)'"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}